From 1ed88c44cdb89fc2bdd68677ca4966ed2a0337fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:25:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 73/73] resolve: a macro body only sees locals declared before
 the macro's definition

A `macro_rules!` body resolves its identifiers in the scope of the
macro's definition. mrustc modelled this with hygiene contexts alone:
a body identifier could see any local whose context is an ancestor of
its own, and every local written directly in the enclosing function
shares that context, whether it was declared before the `macro_rules!`
item or in the arm that invokes the macro. simd-json 0.18.1
(src/stage2.rs) has

    let mut c: u8 = 0;
    ...
    macro_rules! object_continue { () => {{ update_char!(); match c { b',' => .. } }} }
    ...
    StackState::Object { last_start: l, cnt: c } => { ..; object_continue!(); }

and the body's `c` resolved to the arm's `cnt: c` (a usize):

    MACRO<..::object_continue> error:0: Failed to find an impl of
        ::"core-0_0_0"::cmp::PartialEq<u8,> for usize

Record where each `macro_rules!` is defined, tag every expansion's
body hygiene with that position, and keep the declaration position of
each local. When a body identifier can only see a local through an
ancestor context, a local declared definitely later than the
definition (same file, later position) is skipped. Everything parsed
from one expansion reports its invocation's position, so an equal
position (a macro defined inside an expansion using that expansion's
locals) or another file keeps the previous behaviour. An exact hygiene
match (0ab65260) is untouched, and macros deserialised from other
crates record no position, so they resolve as before.

The data lives in a side table keyed by hygiene (macro_rules/def_site.hpp)
rather than in `Ident::Hygiene` itself, so the HIR format and the
widely included headers are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
